data: {"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "**Evaluating Network Findings**\n\nI'm now integrating insights on scientific networks, focusing on the combination of conventional and novel connections. I'm recalling the findings from Uzzi et al. (2013) regarding the impact of atypical combinations with an emphasis on 17.9 million Web of Science papers.\n\nI'm now contrasting this with the work of Wang, Veugelers & Stephan (2017) on novelty biases, citing their work regarding delayed recognition and lower short-term citations for novel combinations, as well as Fontana, Iori, Montobbio & Sinatra (2020) and their measurements of novelty and interdisciplinarity.\n\n\n","thought": true}],"role": "model"},"index": 0}],"usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 588,"totalTokenCount": 9261,"promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT","tokenCount": 588}],"thoughtsTokenCount": 8673,"serviceTier": "standard"},"modelVersion": "gemini-4-neon","responseId": "2gMDa9HmCp2p5NoPmO3w6A4"}

